    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1619a9c7",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a diverse group of people raising their hands in what appears to be a classroom or meeting setting, with the overlaid text reading 'hands up all racists who support white genocide.' This juxtaposition is intentionally provocative and hateful, as it uses a visual of passive, non-threatening participation to frame a call for identifying and condemning individuals based on their race and alleged support for a genocidal ideology. The phrase 'white genocide' is a false and inflammatory conspiracy theory that falsely claims systemic extermination of white populations, which is not only factually baseless but also incites racial hatred and division. The meme's intent is to weaponize the image of collective participation to promote a divisive, racially charged narrative, targeting individuals based on their racial identity and potentially inciting hostility toward them. The visual of people raising hands is typically associated with cooperation or compliance, which contrasts sharply with the hateful and conspiratorial message, creating a jarring and manipulative effect designed to provoke outrage or reinforce extremist ideologies. The meme is therefore classified as hateful, as it directly attacks individuals based on their race and promotes a dangerous, false narrative that can incite violence or discrimination against targeted groups.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_0264ca4f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
